# Dependencies (Poetry)

When a task needs a **new or changed Python package**, the agent does **not** alter the dependency manifest or lockfile. The **user** runs Poetry locally.

## Agent must not run

- `poetry add`, `poetry remove`, `poetry update`, `poetry install`, `poetry lock`
- Editing `pyproject.toml` or `poetry.lock` to add, remove, or bump dependencies (unless the user explicitly asks the agent to edit those files after they ran Poetry themselves)

## What the agent should do

1. **Before** importing a package that is not already in `pyproject.toml`, tell the user which command to run and wait for confirmation (or for the user to say dependencies are installed).
2. Suggest the exact Poetry command:
   - Runtime: `poetry add <package>` (optional version constraint, e.g. `poetry add httpx@^0.27.0`)
   - Dev-only (tests, lint, load tests): `poetry add --group dev <package>`
3. After the user adds dependencies, remind them to refresh the environment used to run the API:
   - **Docker Compose** (default local setup): `make build` — rebuilds images from `pyproject.toml` / `poetry.lock` and restarts containers (`make help`: use after changing dependencies).
   - **Kubernetes / Minikube image** (see `docs/local-deployment.md`): `make build-container` after deps change, inside the Minikube Docker env when applicable.
4. Then implement or continue code that uses the new package and run quality checks (`make format`, `make lint-fix`, `make lint-type`, `make test`) as usual.

## User workflow (reference)

| Step | Command | Who |
| ---- | ------- | --- |
| Add or update package | `poetry add …` / `poetry add --group dev …` / `poetry remove …` | User |
| Rebuild API Docker image (Compose) | `make build` | User (unless they explicitly ask the agent to run it) |
| Rebuild image for K8s local test | `make build-container` | User |
| Apply code + checks | Agent implements; `make test`, etc. | Agent (automatic per quality-checks) |

Poetry updates `pyproject.toml` and `poetry.lock`. The **Dockerfile** runs `poetry install` at image build time, so Compose/K8s images stay in sync only after `make build` or `make build-container`.

## Related boundaries

See **agent-boundaries.mdc** (no `poetry install`, no `make build` / `make start` / deploy unless the user explicitly asks).
